{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/globalidentifier\/storeuri"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"storeURI","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device-local by design: it must never be synced, exported, or adopted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"from another device’s data. Object URIs carry a store UUID and primary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key, so a foreign URI is meaningless here at best — and on a device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restored from another device’s backup (matching store UUID) it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolve to the wrong object. Entries are disposable: a missing or stale","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URI is re-populated wherever the object surfaces next — attach import,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"save capture, or integration creating the object for an insert change.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(An update or delete change whose identifier has no usable URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped for that pass, not re-resolved.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier\/storeURI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:9Ensembles16GlobalIdentifierV8storeURISSSgvp","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","title":"storeURI","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"storeURI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local object’s "},{"code":"NSManagedObjectID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URI — the essential mapping from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this global identifier to its row in THIS device’s persistent store,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used by integration to locate the object for incoming changes."}],"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","type":"topic","title":"Ensembles","abstract":[{"text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/GlobalIdentifier/storeURI":{"title":"storeURI","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local object’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObjectID"},{"type":"text","text":" URI — the essential mapping from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this global identifier to its row in THIS device’s persistent store,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used by integration to locate the object for incoming changes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier\/storeURI","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/globalidentifier\/storeuri","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"storeURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIden